WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.710 --> 00:00:02.830
Hold onto your butts, Bat-fans.

00:00:02.830 --> 00:00:06.720
Director Matt Reeves has shared images of
the new Batmobile from the upcoming reboot

00:00:06.720 --> 00:00:10.950
The Batman, and we think it's pretty safe
to say that they do not disappoint.

00:00:10.950 --> 00:00:14.969
In keeping with past iterations of the iconic
vehicle, the new version looks very lean,

00:00:14.969 --> 00:00:16.930
very mean, and very fast.

00:00:16.930 --> 00:00:19.449
"Show me my car."

00:00:19.449 --> 00:00:23.289
Pretend for a moment you're some lowlife,
up to no good in Gotham City; maybe you're

00:00:23.289 --> 00:00:26.660
pulling off a jewelry store heist, or holding
up an armored truck.

00:00:26.660 --> 00:00:29.359
Is this the absolute last thing you'd want
to see, or what?

00:00:29.359 --> 00:00:30.609
Here's an overhead view:

00:00:30.609 --> 00:00:35.320
Sleek, black, and obviously built for speed,
like if a manta ray were an automobile.

00:00:35.320 --> 00:00:39.130
We're sure you're already sold, but wait,
we saved the best for last:

00:00:39.130 --> 00:00:40.130
Look.

00:00:40.130 --> 00:00:41.130
At.

00:00:41.130 --> 00:00:42.130
That.

00:00:42.130 --> 00:00:45.380
Now that is a car that nobody but Batman would
be capable of driving for more than a block

00:00:45.380 --> 00:00:49.999
without wrapping it around the nearest telephone
pole, sending it sky-high in a ball of rocket

00:00:49.999 --> 00:00:51.640
fuel-fed flames.

00:00:51.640 --> 00:00:55.329
Not only are Batman die-hards bound to be
drooling puddles over these photos, but we're

00:00:55.329 --> 00:00:59.359
thinking that if you're a car person, your
eyes are popping out of your head right now.

00:00:59.359 --> 00:01:01.600
"I gotta get me one of those."

00:01:01.600 --> 00:01:05.480
For starters, you've probably gotten the idea
that Bruce Wayne did not build this car from

00:01:05.480 --> 00:01:07.150
scratch, and you'd be right.

00:01:07.150 --> 00:01:12.520
Our best guess: this vehicle began life as
a 1970 Dodge Challenger, a legendary muscle

00:01:12.520 --> 00:01:16.799
car that made up for what it lacked in handling
ability with raw, screaming power.

00:01:16.799 --> 00:01:20.871
There are a couple of other models it could
be; the Pontiac GTOs of the late '60s come

00:01:20.871 --> 00:01:21.871
to mind.

00:01:21.871 --> 00:01:25.990
But given those deeply recessed headlights,
extremely low profile, and distinctive curves,

00:01:25.990 --> 00:01:28.619
we're pretty sure that Wayne went with a Dodge.

00:01:28.619 --> 00:01:31.280
You'll note, however, that there are a few
modern touches.

00:01:31.280 --> 00:01:35.560
The trapezoidal tail lights, along with the
rear window-mounted third brake light, are

00:01:35.560 --> 00:01:37.110
obvious after-market modifications.

00:01:37.110 --> 00:01:41.549
Also, looking closely at the rear view, you'll
notice there's a small video display mounted

00:01:41.549 --> 00:01:46.369
in-dash; touchscreen GPS units were not in
widespread use at the time The Batman is thought

00:01:46.369 --> 00:01:51.610
to be set, around the mid- to late- 2000s,
but this is Bruce Wayne we're talking about.

00:01:51.610 --> 00:01:52.840
"I'm rich."

00:01:52.840 --> 00:01:56.350
Finally, the engine.

00:01:56.350 --> 00:01:57.880
The freaking engine.

00:01:57.880 --> 00:02:02.799
It looks like an absolutely massive V10, with
enormous vertical exhausts up each side.

00:02:02.799 --> 00:02:04.520
That big ring in the center?

00:02:04.520 --> 00:02:07.750
Afterburner, obviously; you don't want to
stand anywhere near it, ever.

00:02:07.750 --> 00:02:12.270
Oh, and if you're wondering if any '60s or
'70s muscle cars featured rear-mounted engines,

00:02:12.270 --> 00:02:14.530
the answer is, "No, not one of them."

00:02:14.530 --> 00:02:18.880
Why on Earth would Master Bruce have relocated
the engine to the rear of the car?

00:02:18.880 --> 00:02:22.030
Why, to make room for something else under
the hood, of course.

00:02:22.030 --> 00:02:25.850
Something, we're thinking, like a big, fat
array of weapons and/or gadgets.

00:02:25.850 --> 00:02:29.760
Aside from that afterburner, which you know
will just spit a gigantic stream of fire,

00:02:29.760 --> 00:02:33.990
this Batmobile doesn't bear much resemblance
to the iterations we've seen in the past.

00:02:33.990 --> 00:02:37.570
It's the only version we've ever seen that
looks like a modified, commercially available

00:02:37.570 --> 00:02:42.730
vehicle; even the '60s Batmobile was based
on the Lincoln Futura, a concept car that

00:02:42.730 --> 00:02:44.520
was never released to the public.

00:02:44.520 --> 00:02:49.440
The Batmobile driven by Michael Keaton's Caped
Crusader in 1989's Batman was quite obviously

00:02:49.440 --> 00:02:54.380
a custom design, with its enormous size necessary
for concealing all of the "wonderful toys"

00:02:54.380 --> 00:02:55.880
which it could deploy.

00:02:55.880 --> 00:02:59.590
With Christopher Nolan's Dark Knight trilogy,
the Batmobile's design took an even harder

00:02:59.590 --> 00:03:04.370
turn into custom territory; dubbed the "Tumbler,"
it wasn't so much a car as it was a highly

00:03:04.370 --> 00:03:09.090
armored, customizable, multi-configuration
assault vehicle of the type that any military

00:03:09.090 --> 00:03:12.590
worth its salt would shell out millions for.

00:03:12.590 --> 00:03:15.630
"What's that?"

00:03:15.630 --> 00:03:17.810
"Oh, the Tumbler?

00:03:17.810 --> 00:03:21.800
You wouldn't be interested in that."

00:03:21.800 --> 00:03:26.290
In keeping with the DIY, repurposed aesthetic
of the new Batsuit, though, this new Batmobile

00:03:26.290 --> 00:03:31.470
looks a bit like a first draft, an insanely
fast, powerful, kickass first draft, but a

00:03:31.470 --> 00:03:32.920
first draft nonetheless.

00:03:32.920 --> 00:03:36.840
Perhaps Wayne will have upgraded by the time
we see The Batman 2.

00:03:36.840 --> 00:03:41.170
This version, though, looks absolutely ferocious,
and if Bats' legions of fans hadn't whipped

00:03:41.170 --> 00:03:45.050
themselves up into a frenzy over this flick
before, we think it's safe for them to start

00:03:45.050 --> 00:03:46.230
doing so now.

00:03:46.230 --> 00:03:49.100
"Chicks dig the car."

00:03:49.100 --> 00:03:52.060
The Batman hits the big screen on June 25,
2021.

